 "note": "Left side measured on the Getty / LAT photo 'Silverstone 9 June 1991, Gary Ayles' (near side-on, nose left), warped onto the model by the wheel centres and the B- and C-pillar window corners; checked against 'Silverstone 1 April 1991' (Getty / LAT) and the TV graphic drawings. Ayles's left side carries ICS plc and the ICS roundel on the rear quarter (Rouse's car has KALIBER on this side). Stripes, ESSO board, Shell, YOKOHAMA, KONI/CHAMPION placed as on Rouse's car, where they match. Wheels: white 5-spoke as on the team cars in the paddock (no standing photo of #33 itself). Uncertain: the ICS roundel's inner monogram is simplified to the letters ICS.",
